course: dictionary
lesson: 15180
title: Rude words and what they mean
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: You may hear rude words in stories or from angry people. You need to know what they mean, but you do not need to use them. «That scumbag stole my bike!» The word scumbag is an insult. The angry voice and the stolen bike are the clues.
explain: A scumbag is a nasty, dishonest or mean person. When someone says «a total scumbag», they mean the person is very bad. Knowing the meaning helps you understand the story, even when the word is rude.
explain: Rude words can hurt people's feelings, so at school we use polite words instead. Scumbag can be replaced with unkind, dishonest or mean. Choose a word that describes what the person did, not an insult.
fact: A scumbag is a rude slang word for a nasty, dishonest or mean person.
fact: «Scumbag» is an insult, so do not use it at school or with friends.
fact: «A total scumbag» means someone who is very mean or dishonest.
fact: When you meet a rude word in a story, look at what the person did. The actions are the clues.
fact: Polite words to use instead are unkind, dishonest and mean.
exercise: «That scumbag stole my bike!» What does scumbag mean? | A type of bicycle | *A nasty, dishonest or mean person | A kind neighbour who lends bikes | A lost dog
exercise: Mia's mum says, «Never call anyone a scumbag at school.» What does this tell you? | *It is a rude word, so we do not use it at school | It is a word for a small bird | It is a kind word for a good friend | It means a clean and tidy room
exercise: Which polite word could replace scumbag in «That scumbag stole my bike!»? | Sleepy | Lovely | *Dishonest | Tall
test: «He is a total scumbag for lying to his friend.» What does total scumbag mean here? | *Very mean and dishonest | A kind helper who always says sorry | Very tall and happy | A small, quiet animal
test: Why should you not say scumbag at school? | It is only used in old books | *It is rude slang that can hurt people | It is a long and difficult word | It is a very polite word for a friend
exam: Jayden hears a friend shout «scumbag» in the playground. What should he do? | Look it up in a book about animals | Shout it back, because it is only a word | Think it means something kind | *Know it is rude, and do not repeat it at school
